SpecForge (with ExitTrain fork)
================================

This project is a fork of SpecForge (https://github.com/sgl-project/SpecForge)
maintained by the SGLang team, and is distributed under the same MIT license
as the upstream project (see LICENSE).

Upstream copyright:
    Copyright (c) 2025 sgl-project

Modifications and additions in this fork:
    Copyright (c) 2026 The authors of the accompanying ICLR submission

The main additions relative to upstream are:

* A new training method registered as ``strategy: "exittrain"`` implementing
  a full-tree target-verify variant of DTED (Tree-Expected Decoding).
  See specforge/algorithms/exittrain/ and the "ExitTrain" section of README.md.
* Example configurations and launch scripts for reproducing ExitTrain
  training runs on Qwen3-4B, Qwen3-8B, Llama-3.1-8B-Instruct, and
  Qwen3-Coder-30B-A3B-Instruct targets.

All other SpecForge components (algorithms, application layer, config
system, runtime data plane, disaggregated launcher, etc.) are inherited
from upstream and remain under upstream copyright.

Portions of individual source files carry per-file copyright headers with
"Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0" language inherited from
upstream. Those headers describe the *file-level* license SpecForge
originally applied inside its MIT-licensed distribution and are preserved
verbatim for provenance.
